A||||3||GT Bastard||1.52 Comp Cams full-roller rockers. question...||||1||
Z||000000||GT Bastard||02-24-2001||07:59 AM||||I recently scored a set of these(Dad came up short a couple for his smallblock and decided to help me out.)  I went through some previous posts on roller rockers but all I could find was the crane gold 1.6 rockers.  It was mentioned before that 1.6 rockers required different studs, but does that hold true for ANY roller rocker?  Mine are 1.52 and adonized bronze if that helps.  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||batboy||02-24-2001||08:57 AM||||Bastard, I don't have personal experience with installing V8 roller rockers into the V6, but here is a quote from my handy dandy "Chevrolet Power" bible (p. 175):<P>"Aftermarket needle needle bearing rocker arms for a small-block V8 with 7/16-inch trunions should be installed on cast iron V6/60 cylinder heads that have been converted to 7/16-inch rocker studs. Due to limited clearance between adjacent rocker arms, narrow aluminum rockers are required."<P>I've heard that there aren't many roller rockers that are narrow enough to fit the V6.<BR> I've also heard of people doing a little grinding on the rockers to make them fit, but I'd be very careful about doing that. Clearances in the valvetrain need to be perfect, especially at high RPM.||||reg||1
Z||000002||terryk||02-24-2001||01:46 PM||||Crane Hi-Intensity 1.5 Roller Rockers - 11756-12 ~$250<P>Crane Aluminum 1.5 Roller Rockers - 25750-12 ~$250<P>I believe the 11756-12 are what I had on my X-11 with Fiero valve covers (they fit), but call Crane and check. They stud do need to be replaced. Very nice rockers.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Shaun41178||02-24-2001||06:22 PM||||i think the small block rocker studs are 3/8 inch and the big block are 7/16 inch.<P>either way they won't fit on the fiero stud as the Fiero stud is 10 mm.<P>The Crane full roller rocker for a fiero is up to $360 I think.  i called Summit and that is what they quoted me like a year or so ago.<P>What you can do is buy cheap roller tip rockers for a small block and those cost like around $90. i think and can even get a 1.6 ratio.  then just use your 10 mm nuts and rocker balls with the V8 rockers.  it has been done with success so that is another option.||||reg||1
